      "content": "Given:\n- Lorie has 2 pieces of $100 bills.\n- One $100 bill is changed into $50 bills.\n- Half of the remaining $100 bill is changed to $10 bills, and the rest is changed to $5 bills.\n\nUnknown:\n- The total number of pieces of bills Lorie will have after the changes.\n\nStep-by-step solution:\n1. **Change one $100 bill into $50 bills:**\n   - $100 ÷ $50 = 2 pieces of $50 bills.\n\n2. **After changing one $100 bill, Lorie has:**\n   - 2 pieces of $50 bills.\n   - 1 piece of $100 bill remaining.\n\n3. **Change half of the remaining $100 bill to $10 bills:**\n   - Half of $100 is $50.\n   - $50 ÷ $10 = 5 pieces of $10 bills.\n\n4. **Change the rest of the remaining $100 bill to $5 bills:**\n   - The rest of the $100 bill is also $50.\n   - $50 ÷ $5 = 10 pieces of $5 bills.\n\n5. **Total number of pieces of bills:**\n   - 2 pieces of $50 bills + 5 pieces of $10 bills + 10 pieces of $5 bills = 17 pieces of bills.\n\nFinal check:\n- The problem asks for the total number of pieces of bills, and the calculation shows 17 pieces.\n- The given problem and the operations are correctly followed.\n\nFINAL: 17",
